<!--
	Performers: the Swordsinger and Bladedancer lines (Swordsinger, Sword Muse, Bladedancer,
	Spectral Dancer). Glittering Medals (CustomBuffBook) teach every class the songs and
	dances, so these are what a medal can't give. They are in the class skill trees and are
	learned from the Grand Masters like any class skill. See README "Performers" and
	config/Custom/Performers.ini (Virtuoso: their songs and dances last longer, and stacking
	them doesn't cost them extra MP).

	27500-27508  Swordsinger line: the battle bard, who keeps the party standing.
	27520-27528  Bladedancer line: the war dancer, who tears the enemy down.

	PERFORMANCES (toggles, one at a time: they share abnormalType PERFORMANCE, abnormalLevel 1,
	so turning one on replaces the other whatever their levels). While on, the PerformanceAura
	effect keeps an "echo" on everyone in range every tick (5 ticks = about 3.3 seconds):
	  * affects PARTY: the performer, the party and their summons within 900. A buff, in the
	    triggered-buff bar (isTriggeredSkill), so it never pushes out a buff or a dance.
	  * affects ENEMY: monsters (and players the performer could attack without forcing it)
	    within 400 and in sight. A debuff, rolled once with its own activateRate, then held.
	  The echo lasts 10 seconds and is extended while the target stays in range, so it fades a
	  few seconds after leaving it, and turning the performance off takes it away at once.
	  Echoes have their own abnormalType: they stack with every retail buff and medal song,
	  and the same echo from two performers doesn't (the higher level holds it).
	  A stunned, sleeping or paralyzed performer stops performing until it ends.
	  Levels: 1 at the 2nd class, 2 later in it, 3 at the 3rd class.

	STANCES (toggles, one at a time: abnormalType PERFORMER_STANCE). A self stance with an
	on-hit trigger (TriggerSkillByDamageDealt, normal attacks only). A stance and a performance
	can be on together. Levels 1-3 at the 2nd class, 4 at the 3rd class.

	FINALES: one big 3rd class skill each, on a long reuse.

	MP: performances drain 0.3 and stances 0.2 x (level - 1) / 7.5 MP per second
	(MpConsumePerLevel, like 312 Vicious Stance at 0.8), about 3 and 2 MP per second at 76.

	Keep custom skill ids below 32768. The client needs Skillname-e.dat / Skillgrp.dat rows for
	every id here (client/Performers), or it shows the skill without a name or icon. The icons
	are retail icons of performer skills the medals don't teach, so an echo is never mistaken
	for a medal song in the buff bar.
-->
<list xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="../../../xsd/skills.xsd">

